# Netlify redirect rules. First match wins.

# One canonical host. The `!` is required: without it Netlify skips a redirect
# whenever a real file exists at the path, which here is every path.
https://c64ready.netlify.app/*  https://c64ready.com/:splat  301!

# Extensionless docs URLs (/docs/about) are resolved to the .html file by
# Netlify's asset server itself, before the redirect engine sees them, so they
# need no rule here — and must not get one: Netlify matches a request against the
# file it resolves to, so `/docs/index.html -> /docs/` fired on /docs/ as well and
# redirected it to itself. <link rel="canonical"> is what points crawlers at the
# .html URL that sitemap.xml and the precache (src/sw.js) use.

# The Datasette animation was a .gif that no service worker precached, so a docs
# page held in an older precache still requests it over the network. Keep the old
# name resolving until those clients have taken an update.
/guide/datasette-loading.gif  /guide/datasette-loading.webp  301

# The 3D assets moved into /models/. A client still running the previous build
# (it waits on the update prompt) asks for them at the site root; keep those
# names resolving until such clients have taken an update.
/commodore_64.glb          /models/commodore_64.glb          301
/commodore_64_4k.glb       /models/commodore_64_4k.glb       301
/bedroom.glb               /models/bedroom.glb               301
/bedroom_small.glb         /models/bedroom_small.glb         301
/bedroom_light.webp        /models/bedroom_light.webp        301
/bedroom_light_small.webp  /models/bedroom_light_small.webp  301

# The CLI guide became a topic page of the User Guide. Its heading ids did not
# change, and a browser keeps the #fragment across the redirect.
/docs/user-guide-cli.html  /docs/guide-cli.html  301
/docs/user-guide-cli       /docs/guide-cli.html  301

/docs/userport-devices.html  /docs/device-plugins.html  301
/docs/userport-devices       /docs/device-plugins.html  301
